<div class="chat-workspace" id="chat-tester" data-api-base="{{ rtrim($baseUrl, '/').'/' }}" data-health-url="{{ route('developer.socket.health') }}">
    <header class="chat-heading">
        <div><span class="chat-breadcrumb">Developer tools / WebSockets</span><h2 id="chat-view-title" tabindex="-1">Getting started</h2><p id="chat-view-description">A simple, step-by-step workspace for testing live chat.</p></div>
        <div class="chat-heading-actions"><span class="category-badge" id="chat-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Disconnected</span><a class="btn" href="#realtime/full" data-tab="realtime" data-chat-view="full">Run full check →</a></div>
    </header>
    <p class="chat-session-bar" id="chat-metrics" role="status" aria-live="polite">Socket: — · Transport: — · Last ping: — · Sent: 0 · Received: 0</p>

    <div data-chat-views="ping conversations send receive history session end events" hidden><div class="flow-note" id="chat-needs-connection" style="margin-bottom:16px">Socket actions need a connected user. <a href="#realtime/connection" data-tab="realtime" data-chat-view="connection">Connect &amp; verify your user →</a></div></div>
    <section data-chat-views="overview">
        <div class="flow-note"><strong>Test one step at a time.</strong> Choose an option under WebSockets in the sidebar. Start with your connection, then send a message and check it in another participant's tab. Each step includes a sample response, so you can explore before connecting.</div>
        <div class="chat-start-cards">
            <a class="chat-start-card" href="#realtime/connection" data-tab="realtime" data-chat-view="connection"><span>01</span><div><h3>Connect &amp; verify</h3><p>Set your server URL, paste a user token and establish a connection.</p></div></a>
            <a class="chat-start-card" href="#realtime/ping" data-tab="realtime" data-chat-view="ping"><span>02</span><div><h3>Check the connection</h3><p>Send a ping, see round-trip time or turn on automatic checks.</p></div></a>
            <a class="chat-start-card" href="#realtime/conversations" data-tab="realtime" data-chat-view="conversations"><span>03</span><div><h3>Choose a conversation</h3><p>Load your inbox or start a conversation with a teacher or institute.</p></div></a>
            <a class="chat-start-card" href="#realtime/send" data-tab="realtime" data-chat-view="send"><span>04</span><div><h3>Send a message</h3><p>Compose a real test message and inspect its acknowledgement.</p></div></a>
            <a class="chat-start-card" href="#realtime/receive" data-tab="realtime" data-chat-view="receive"><span>05</span><div><h3>Receive messages</h3><p>Watch incoming messages here while sending from another tab.</p></div></a>
            <a class="chat-start-card" href="#realtime/full" data-tab="realtime" data-chat-view="full"><span>✓</span><div><h3>Run the full check</h3><p>Check the flow from connection to disconnect with a result for each step.</p></div></a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <details class="panel chat-settings" id="chat-connection-settings" data-chat-views="connection ping conversations send receive history session end events full">
        <summary>Connection settings <small>Your server and user token · shared across all steps</small></summary>
        <div class="panel-body chat-settings-grid">
            <div class="field"><label for="chat-url">Socket server URL</label><input class="control" id="chat-url" type="url" placeholder="https://chat.example.com" data-chat-config><p class="hint">Host and port only — leave out /nearby_teachers/public. Use this website's origin only when a WebSocket reverse proxy is configured. HTTPS requires a working TLS endpoint.</p></div>
            <div class="field"><label for="chat-path">Socket path</label><input class="control" id="chat-path" value="/socket.io/" autocomplete="off" data-chat-config><p class="hint">Usually /socket.io/ — change only if your proxy uses a different path.</p></div>
            <div class="field"><label for="chat-token">User login token</label><input class="control" id="chat-token" type="password" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Paste a learner, teacher or institute token" data-chat-config><div class="chat-actions"><button class="btn" id="chat-use-token" type="button" data-chat-config>Use API explorer token</button></div><p class="hint">Kept in this page only. To change accounts while connected, disconnect from Leave &amp; end test.</p></div>
        </div>
    </details>

    <section class="panel" data-chat-views="connection"><div class="panel-body chat-step-intro"><h3>Let's connect your user</h3><p>Check the chat service, verify your token, then connect. A successful connection lets you send pings and use conversation events.</p><div class="chat-actions"><button class="btn" id="chat-health" type="button" data-chat-action>1. Check server</button><button class="btn" id="chat-authorize" type="button" data-chat-action>2. Verify token</button><button class="btn btn-primary" id="chat-connect" type="button" data-chat-action>3. Connect user</button></div><p class="chat-note">Server check tests the configured internal service. Connect tests the public URL above. HTTPS pages need an HTTPS socket URL.</p></div></section>
    <section class="panel" data-chat-views="ping" hidden><div class="panel-body chat-step-intro"><h3>Is your connection responding?</h3><p>Ping sends a small check to the server. The response shows how long the round trip took. Auto ping repeats every 5 seconds.</p><div class="chat-actions"><button class="btn btn-primary" id="chat-ping" type="button" data-chat-connected data-chat-action disabled>Send a ping</button><button class="btn" id="chat-ping-start" type="button" data-chat-connected data-chat-action disabled>Start auto ping</button><button class="btn" id="chat-ping-stop" type="button" disabled>Stop auto ping</button></div><p class="chat-note">Automatic heartbeat ping/pong appears in the event log. Ping checks connectivity; it does not prove that messages are being saved or delivered.</p></div></section>

    <section class="panel" data-chat-views="conversations send receive history end events full" hidden><div class="panel-body">
        <div class="chat-context-grid">
            <div class="field"><label for="chat-conversation">Conversation ID</label><input class="control" id="chat-conversation" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Paste a conversation UUID" data-chat-flow-input><p class="hint">Shared between these steps. Find an ID in Conversations → Load my inbox.</p></div>
            <div class="field" data-chat-views="conversations history"><label for="chat-inbox-select">Choose from your inbox</label><select class="control" id="chat-inbox-select" data-chat-flow-input><option value="">Load your inbox to see conversations</option></select><p class="hint">Selecting a conversation fills its ID automatically.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="field" data-chat-views="send events full" data-chat-event-field="body" hidden style="margin-top:18px"><label for="chat-body">Your test message</label><textarea class="control" id="chat-body" rows="3" placeholder="Write a message for the other participant…" data-chat-flow-input></textarea><p class="hint">Sending saves a real message. After an acknowledgement timeout, check saved history before retrying.</p></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="panel" data-chat-views="conversations" hidden><div class="panel-body chat-step-intro"><h3>Find or start a conversation</h3><p>Load your inbox and choose a conversation above. You can check your access and join its live room.</p><div class="chat-actions"><button class="btn btn-primary" id="chat-inbox" type="button" data-chat-action>Load my inbox</button><button class="btn" id="chat-room-auth" type="button" data-chat-action>Check my access</button><button class="btn" id="chat-join" type="button" data-chat-connected data-chat-action disabled>Join conversation</button></div><details class="chat-protocol" style="margin-top:22px"><summary>Need a new conversation? · Learners only</summary><div class="field"><label for="chat-provider">Teacher or institute user ID</label><input class="control" id="chat-provider" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Provider user UUID" data-chat-config><p class="hint">Creates or reuses a conversation. No message is sent yet.</p></div><button class="btn" id="chat-start" type="button" data-chat-action>Start / find conversation</button></details></div></section>
    <section class="panel" data-chat-views="send" hidden><div class="panel-body chat-step-intro"><h3>Send your message</h3><p>Use the socket to test live chat, or REST to test the HTTP send API. Choose one method for each test message.</p><div class="chat-actions"><button class="btn btn-primary" id="chat-send" type="button" data-chat-connected data-chat-action disabled>Send via socket</button><button class="btn" id="chat-rest-send" type="button" data-chat-action>Send via REST</button></div><p class="chat-note">Both methods save messages to the database. An acknowledgement confirms the save. Check Receive messages in a second participant's tab to verify delivery.</p></div></section>
    <section class="panel" data-chat-views="receive" hidden><div class="panel-body chat-step-intro"><h3>Your live inbox</h3><p>Connect this tab with the receiving user's token, then send from the other participant's tab. Messages appear here automatically — no Receive API call is needed.</p><div class="chat-listening" id="chat-listening-status" role="status">Connect a user to start listening.</div><div class="chat-messages" id="chat-message-feed" aria-live="polite"><p class="chat-note">No live messages received yet. A mock event is shown below.</p></div><p class="chat-note">Only the latest 30 unique live messages are shown here. These are page observations; use Saved history to check persisted messages.</p></div></section>
    <section class="panel" data-chat-views="events" hidden><div class="panel-body chat-step-intro">
        <h3 id="chat-event-title">Chat events</h3><p id="chat-event-description">Choose an event from the sidebar or the operation selector below.</p>
        <div class="chat-event-grid" style="margin-top:16px">
            <div class="field" data-chat-event-field="messageId"><label for="chat-event-message">Message ID</label><input class="control" id="chat-event-message" placeholder="Message UUID from history" data-chat-flow-input></div>
            <div class="field" data-chat-event-field="replyToId"><label for="chat-event-reply">Reply to message ID</label><input class="control" id="chat-event-reply" placeholder="Original message UUID" data-chat-flow-input></div>
            <div class="field" data-chat-event-field="reaction"><label for="chat-event-reaction">Reaction</label><select class="control" id="chat-event-reaction" data-chat-flow-input><option value="👍">👍 Like</option><option value="❤️">❤️ Love</option><option value="😂">😂 Laugh</option><option value="😮">😮 Surprise</option><option value="😢">😢 Sad</option><option value="🙏">🙏 Thanks</option><option value="🎉">🎉 Celebrate</option><option value="👎">👎 Dislike</option><option value="">Remove my reaction</option></select></div>
            <div class="field" data-chat-event-field="perPage"><label for="chat-event-page">Messages per page</label><input class="control" id="chat-event-page" type="number" min="1" max="100" value="20" data-chat-flow-input></div>
            <div class="field" data-chat-event-field="cursor"><label for="chat-event-cursor">Next cursor (optional)</label><input class="control" id="chat-event-cursor" placeholder="pagination.nextCursor from previous response" data-chat-flow-input></div>
        </div>
        <div class="chat-actions"><button class="btn btn-primary" id="chat-event-run" type="button" data-chat-connected data-chat-action disabled>Run socket event</button><button class="btn" id="chat-event-rest" type="button" data-chat-action>Run REST API</button></div>
        <p class="chat-note" id="chat-event-note">All actions enforce the real participant permissions. Mutations affect real application data.</p>
    </div></section>
    <section class="panel" data-chat-views="history" hidden><div class="panel-body chat-step-intro"><h3>Check what was saved</h3><p>Load the latest 20 saved messages for the selected conversation. Use this after a send timeout to check whether your message was saved.</p><div class="chat-actions"><button class="btn btn-primary" id="chat-history" type="button" data-chat-action>Load saved history</button></div></div></section>
    <section class="panel" data-chat-views="session" hidden><div class="panel-body chat-step-intro"><h3>Understand connection changes</h3><p>Reconnect attempts, connection errors and session expiry are observed automatically. Watch the event log below while the connection changes.</p><div class="flow-note" style="margin-top:15px">On session expiry, reconnect with a valid login token. After reconnecting, reload saved history and rejoin the conversation. Automatic retries stop after 3 attempts.</div><div class="chat-actions"><a class="btn" href="#realtime/connection" data-tab="realtime" data-chat-view="connection">Go to connection →</a></div><p class="chat-note">Session expiry is a server event and can take up to 15 minutes. This panel does not force an expiry.</p></div></section>
    <section class="panel" data-chat-views="end" hidden><div class="panel-body chat-step-intro"><h3>Finish your test</h3><p>Leave the selected conversation room, or disconnect this user to end the socket session and stop auto ping.</p><div class="chat-actions"><button class="btn" id="chat-leave" type="button" data-chat-connected data-chat-action disabled>Leave conversation</button><button class="btn btn-primary" id="chat-disconnect" type="button" data-chat-action disabled>Disconnect &amp; end test</button></div><p class="chat-note">Leaving a conversation still allows private user-room delivery. Disconnecting closes this socket; it does not delete messages, remove the conversation or log the account out.</p></div></section>
    <section class="panel" data-chat-views="full" hidden><div class="panel-body chat-step-intro"><h3>Check the complete flow</h3><p>With a token and existing conversation ID, this checks the server, authorization, connection, ping, join, history, leave and disconnect. Each step gets its own result.</p><label class="chat-send-choice"><input id="chat-flow-send" type="checkbox" data-chat-flow-input><span><strong>Also send one real test message</strong><br>Verifies its acknowledgement, matching live event and saved history. Leave unchecked for a check without sending messages.</span></label><div class="chat-actions"><button class="btn btn-primary" id="chat-run" type="button">Run full check</button><button class="btn" id="chat-stop" type="button" disabled>Stop check</button></div><ol class="chat-checklist" id="chat-checklist" aria-label="Full check results" aria-live="polite"></ol><p class="chat-note">This opens a fresh connection and disconnects when finished. Stopping cannot undo a message already submitted.</p></div></section>

    <nav class="chat-next" id="chat-step-navigation" aria-label="Previous and next WebSocket step" hidden><a id="chat-previous" href="#realtime/overview" data-tab="realtime" data-chat-view="overview">← Getting started</a><a id="chat-next" href="#realtime/connection" data-tab="realtime" data-chat-view="connection">Next: Connect &amp; verify →</a></nav>
    <section class="panel" data-chat-views="connection ping conversations send receive history session end events full" hidden><div class="panel-body chat-result-grid">
        <div><details class="chat-protocol" open><summary>Request &amp; event details</summary><div class="field"><label for="chat-operation">Operation</label><select class="control" id="chat-operation"></select><p class="hint" id="chat-operation-help"></p></div><pre class="chat-code" id="chat-request-example" aria-label="Example request"></pre></details></div>
        <div><div class="chat-result-heading"><strong>Response</strong><button class="btn" id="chat-show-mock" type="button">Show mock</button></div><p class="hint" id="chat-result-label" role="status">Mock response · fictional</p><pre class="chat-code" id="chat-result" aria-live="polite"></pre></div>
    </div></section>
    <details class="panel chat-log-panel" id="chat-log-panel" data-chat-views="connection ping conversations send receive history session end events full" hidden><summary>Event log <small>Requests, acknowledgements and live events · credentials redacted</small></summary><div class="panel-body"><div class="chat-actions" style="margin:0 0 12px"><button class="btn" id="chat-clear" type="button">Clear log</button><button class="btn" id="chat-copy-log" type="button">Copy log</button><button class="btn" id="chat-copy-example" type="button">Copy app connection example</button></div><pre class="chat-code" id="chat-log" aria-label="Socket events and acknowledgements">No socket events yet.</pre></div></details>
    <p class="chat-note" data-chat-views="connection ping conversations send receive history session end events full" hidden>Live chat tester · Messages sent here affect real application data. Your browser origin must be allowed by the chat server. Never paste a server shared secret.</p>
